===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|cytology}} A male [[gametocyte]], from which a [[spermatozoon]] develops.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013| title=Genome Analysis in Eukaryotes|author=Rabindra N. Chatterjee; Lucas Sanchez |page=71|passage=The spermatogonia continue to reside in the gonocyst and form '''spermatocyte''', which begins to increase in size.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=August 26, 2015|author=|title=A Catalog of Proteins Expressed in the AG Secreted Fluid during the Mature Phase of the Chinese Mitten Crabs ( Eriocheir sinensis )|journal=PLOS ONE|url=http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0136266|doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0136266|volume=|issue=|pages=
|passage=Fragments of laminin chains can act as biologically active peptides to perturb the blood–testis barrier (BTB) permeability function by accelerating protein endocytosis (e.g., occludin) at the site, thereby destabilizing the BTB integrity to facilitate the transit of preleptotene '''spermatocytes'''.}}

